{"title":"2006 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> has a radius of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />. Circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> has a circumference of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/7/687f96b39c84e910c79ea3168d73c3f848ebf51b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 \\pi$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />. Circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> has an area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/e/4eecdd4830005f7b13a04a16c1019a4c3dac062e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 \\pi$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />. List the circles in order from smallest to the largest radius. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/3/27334c7953966e3536ab9b6dcd912f903d1096ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ X, Y, Z\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ Z, X, Y\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ Y, X, Z\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ Z, Y, X\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ X, Z, Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"592\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Not using the formulas of circles, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/5/9851d4e4b945c2d66bc7208893309faca7fe4639.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C=2 \\pi r$\" width=\"66\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/f/28fd4ada92122eb6c326643ac834eac604153366.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A= \\pi r^2$\" width=\"63\" height=\"15\" />, we find that circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> has a radius of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> has a radius of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Also, circle X has a radius of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />. Thus, the order from smallest to largest radius is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/0/31036fb4bd260d86e8ec282cf64869a0a876b8f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ Z, X, Y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"104\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/J5-hDWd28tM\">https://youtu.be/J5-hDWd28tM</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/